# Backend Java

Base package: `com.dev001.itviec`

## Layer separation

| Layer | Location | Responsibility |
|-------|----------|----------------|
| Controller | `controller/` | HTTP mapping, `@Valid` on request body |
| Service | `service/`, `service/impl/` | Business logic |
| Repository | `repository/` | JPA data access |
| Entity | `entity/` | JPA entities |
| DTO | `dto/request`, `dto/response` | API contracts |
| Mapper | `mapper/` | Entity ↔ DTO conversion |
| Validator | `validator/` | Custom validation annotations |

## API response wrapper

All endpoints return `ApiResponse<T>`:

```java
return ApiResponse.<SomeResponse>builder()
    .code(1000)
    .result(someResponse)
    .build();
```

- Base path: `/api/v1/...`
- Use `@RequiredArgsConstructor` + `private final` injection (Lombok)
- Request DTOs: validation annotations; custom validators in `validator/`
- Exceptions: `AppException` — do not swallow errors in controllers

## When adding endpoints

1. Request/Response DTO
2. Service interface + impl
3. Mapper if entity mapping needed
4. Controller method
5. Update frontend types + service if contract changes
